# Dinçer development branch policy

This PC is Dinçer’s primary Talepo machine. Apply on every development task.

## Namespaces

- Dinçer new work: `feature/dincer-<iş-adı>` only. Never `feature/<iş>` for Dinçer work.
- Tuğrul: `feature/tugrul-*` — do not develop, commit, merge, delete, force-push, or rewrite.
- Integration: `cursor/talepo-web-core-platform` — not a daily working branch. Never merge/push there without an explicit user instruction.

Examples: `feature/dincer-personal-opportunity-matching-v1`, `feature/dincer-price-intelligence-v2`.

## Start a new feature

1. Preflight and report: CURRENT BRANCH, HEAD, REMOTE HEAD, WORKING TREE, UNTRACKED, LOCAL-ONLY COMMITS, REMOTE DRIFT, relation to `origin/cursor/talepo-web-core-platform`.
2. `git fetch origin`. Create the new branch from the current integration checkpoint:
   `git switch cursor/talepo-web-core-platform` → `git pull --ff-only` → `git switch -c feature/dincer-<iş-adı>`.
3. If the working tree is dirty, remote has drifted, unexpected commits exist, or fast-forward is impossible: STOP and report. No destructive git.

Keep independent large features on separate branches. Keep a chain only when the work is a natural continuation of the same feature.

## Parallel safety

Before coding, identify files you will touch. If another active branch also changes PanelShell, Prisma schema, entitlements/plans, request understanding, canonical request flow, Opportunity engine, Price Intelligence, shared metadata, auth, or shared UI primitives, report `PARALLEL CONFLICT RISK: HIGH`. Do not edit the other developer’s branch because of that.

If Tuğrul’s work has landed on integration, check divergence before continuing. Plan a safe include of integration; never auto-resolve conflicts. Inspect each conflict; do not drop existing product behavior.

## Commits, push, merge

- Conventional commits (`feat|fix|refactor|test|chore`). Do not put the developer name in the message.
- Push Dinçer work to `origin/feature/dincer-<iş-adı>`. Verify LOCAL HEAD == REMOTE HEAD. Force push is forbidden unless the user explicitly approves.
- Do not auto-merge to `main` or `cursor/talepo-web-core-platform`. Run tests/build, report, wait for an explicit integration instruction.

## Secrets and artifacts

Never commit `.env`, `.env.local`, secrets, `node_modules`, logs, screenshots, or temp artifacts. Never print secret values. Never delete or rewrite env files when switching branches.

## Forbidden without explicit approval

`git reset --hard`, `git clean -fd`, `git push --force` / `--force-with-lease`, branch delete, history rewrite, destructive rebase. If user work could be lost: STOP.

## Checkpoint report (every development close)

